=== Second check, run before the PR ===

The first check above compared line ranges. This one asks the only
question that matters to the open branch: can it still merge?

  git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD refactor/paper-policy-out-of-the-ticket

  Auto-merging crates/app/src/app.rs        <- clean
  Auto-merging crates/app/src/main.rs       <- clean
  Auto-merging crates/app/src/tab.rs        <- clean
  CONFLICT (content): crates/guards/size-baseline.txt

app.rs merges with no conflict, which is the claim the mission made
when it chose these four groups. The one conflict is the size baseline,
where both branches rewrite the !budget line and the comment above it.
It is not a code conflict and it has a mechanical resolution: whichever
branch lands second re-runs 'cargo run -p quantick-guards -- --tighten'
and keeps both comments. Stated in the PR body as blast radius.
